10:/// gh-1605 REG/eval: the mechanics behind the FinalizeGate "grader
11:/// parity" named check. The TB-2.1 verifier runs produced entry points
12:/// itself — typically `subprocess.run([sys.executable, script])` from a
13:/// different working directory with a fresh environment — while the
14:/// agent's self-check runs them from its own session cwd with its
15:/// session env. The modernize-scientific-stack__nwbgy7a trial passed
16:/// every in-session checklist item and still scored 0.0: the verifier's
17:/// clean run collapsed Station 102 to Station 101's mean because the
18:/// script resolved its dataset via the CWD. The check's prescribed
19:/// procedure — re-run each produced entry point from a neutral cwd in a
20:/// fresh subprocess with the session exports stripped, and diff stdout,
21:/// stderr and exit code against the in-session run — must CATCH that
22:/// divergence (the parity ledger item is `fail`, never `pass`) and must
23:/// NOT false-positive a cwd/env-independent entry point (`pass`).
