# Thread 3 — the nwbgy7a evidence fixture lives in two test files

Fixed with the shared fixture helper (the stronger of the two options offered).

**What changed:**

- New `test/support/nwbgy7a_fixture.dart` (the repo's shared-test-support location, like `scripted_stream_harness.dart`) — the single source of truth for the evidence shape:
  - `nwbgy7aStationsCsv` / `nwbgy7aStationsCsvStale` — the fixed dataset (30.3) and the stale fallback (15.5);
  - `nwbgy7aMeanSh` — the cwd-dependent `mean.sh` body (relative dataset resolution + awk aggregation);
  - `writeNwbgy7aFixture(dir)` — the REG layer's Dart writer;
  - `nwbgy7aProduceCommand()` — the IT layer's turn-1 bash command (dataset `printf`s + quoted heredoc), **derived from the same consts**, so the bash-produced fixture provably matches the Dart-written one.
- `test/agent/finalize_gate_grader_parity_test.dart` (REG-1) calls `writeNwbgy7aFixture(appDir)`; `test/integration/fa_finalize_gate_test.dart` (IT-3 turn 1) interpolates `nwbgy7aProduceCommand()`. Each file's comment cross-references the sibling layer and the helper.

A third divergence axis is now a one-file edit.

